  "comments": "<p><strong><u>Notes</u></strong></p><ul><li>According to <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer ugc\" href=\"https://en.numista.com/literature/volume.php?id=9827\"><i><u>“A Numismatic History of the Birmingham Mint”</u></i></a><i> , </i>for 1 millieme AH 1357/1938 coin: “Minted in 1938 (820,000), 1939 (9,180,000), 1942 (12,400,000) and 1943 (3,840,000)” However apparently the date was freezed.</li><li>Although 3 Mints produced this coin, No mint mark was provided for any. &nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Varieties:</u></strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1938 (١٩٣٨-١٣٥٧) has 2 varieties:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/64e67fe7ee3db.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/64e67fe7ee3db.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>Variant 1: With small tails.<br>Variant 2: With large tails.</p>",
